<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#brazilwood">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brazilwood</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brazilwood is a tropical tree whose dense red heartwood was valued in early modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> as the source of a red dye for textiles. It was the first major export of Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, and the colony was named after it. The brazilwood trade was a royal monopoly in the early economy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> became dominant.</p></div>
